1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:03,943
Chapter twenty — the service catalog.

2
00:00:04,003 --> 00:00:18,434
A process is not a service. A
service is what the business buys.

3
00:00:18,494 --> 00:00:29,938
A service is a business capability: a process, plus
the people who run it, plus the software behind it.

4
00:00:29,998 --> 00:00:37,188
Publish this organization and it becomes one.

5
00:00:37,248 --> 00:00:51,511
Rolled up: what it costs a month, how
long it takes, and how capable it is.

6
00:00:51,571 --> 00:00:58,788
Sort the catalog by cost —

7
00:00:58,848 --> 00:01:05,260
— by cycle time —

8
00:01:05,320 --> 00:01:14,765
— or by sigma, to find the service
that fails people most often.

9
00:01:14,825 --> 00:01:25,882
That is a portfolio view an
executive can actually use.

10
00:01:25,942 --> 00:01:37,321
And a new one can be designed the
same way everything else here is.

11
00:01:37,381 --> 00:01:44,383
Cost, cycle time and capability
— per service, from the model.
